@page "/privacy"
@{
  ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy — Queenzone";
  ViewData["Description"] = "How Queenzone collects, uses, and protects your information.";
  ViewData["CanonicalPath"] = "/privacy";
}

<partial name="_PageHero" model='@(("Your Data", "Privacy Policy", "A plain-English explanation of what we collect, why, and how you stay in control.", "Last updated 23 September 2026"))' />

<section class="qz-section qz-section--warm">
  <div class="qz-container qz-container--text">

    <p class="lede">Queenzone is an independent fan archive. This page explains, in plain English, what information we collect when you use the site, why we collect it, and what choices you have.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Queenzone (queenzone.org) is a fan-run archive of news, articles, photography, discography and community history. We are not affiliated with Queen or its representatives. If you have questions about this policy, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@queenzone.org">privacy@queenzone.org</a>.</p>

    <h2>Information you give us</h2>
    <p>If you create a member account, we store your email address, display name and (if you sign up with a password rather than a social login) a securely hashed password. We never store your password in plain text.</p>
    <p>If you send a message from the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page, we store the name, email address, topic, and message you submit so we can reply and keep a record of the request.</p>
    <p>You can also sign in using a Google, Microsoft, Discord, GitHub, Apple, or Queenzone.org account. When you do, the provider shares your name and email address with us so we can create or match your account — we don't receive your password or post on your behalf.</p>
    <p>If you post in the forum, that content (along with your display name) is visible to other visitors, including in the public archive.</p>

    <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
    <p>On the website, we use Google Analytics to understand how people use the site — things like which pages are visited and roughly how long people stay. This data is aggregated and not used to identify you personally.</p>
    <p>On the website, we may show advertising through Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads based on your visits to this and other sites. You can manage ad personalisation through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Ads Settings</a>.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use a small number of cookies on the website to keep you signed in and to support analytics and advertising as described above. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; doing so may sign you out or affect site features.</p>

    <h2>Our mobile app</h2>
    <p>The Queenzone mobile app does not use Google Analytics, Google AdSense, advertising, or cross-app tracking. It uses Sentry for crash and performance diagnostics. If you consent, it uses TelemetryDeck to count anonymous active app installations, visits to the five main sections, and coarse country or device-region information. TelemetryDeck receives a random installation identifier that its SDK hashes before transmission; we do not send your member ID, email, content, searches, or precise location. This data is used only to improve the app and is not linked to your Queenzone account or shared for advertising.</p>
    <p>You can refuse analytics when first asked, or grant or withdraw consent later under Profile → Analytics preferences. Withdrawal stops future collection and deletes the analytics identifier stored on your device. Previously sent events are anonymous and cannot be matched back to you for individual deletion. TelemetryDeck currently has no guaranteed cold-storage deletion schedule and says it expects to delete anonymous events after 7–10 years.</p>
    <p>You can sign in to the app using a Google, Microsoft, Discord, GitHub or Apple account, and manage notifications or delete your account from Settings within the app.</p>

    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To create and maintain your member account, and let you sign in.</li>
      <li>To display forum posts and other content you choose to publish.</li>
      <li>To understand site usage and improve the archive.</li>
      <li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse.</li>
      <li>To respond to messages you send us through the Contact form.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2>Archive content from the legacy site</h2>
    <p>Queenzone is rebuilding a long-running fan site. Public archive content — news, articles, forum posts and similar — may be carried forward from the original site. Private account data (such as passwords or private messages) is not migrated; affected users are invited to create a new account.</p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>We share information only with the service providers who help us run the site and app — for example, our hosting provider, Google Analytics and Google AdSense (website only), Sentry and TelemetryDeck (mobile app only), and the sign-in providers you choose to use (Google, Microsoft, Discord, GitHub, Apple). We require these providers to protect information consistently with this policy. We don't share your data with anyone else except where required by law.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can update your display name or delete your account from <a href="/account/settings">Account settings</a>.</li>
      <li>You can ask us what personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it.</li>
      <li>You can opt out of analytics cookies using your browser's privacy controls or a browser extension.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>When you choose Delete my account, we immediately disable sign-in, hide your profile and avatar, and start removing your personal data and modern contributions. Forum posts and private messages become deleted placeholders. Uploaded media and any Sign in with Apple token are removed by a retrying background process if they cannot be removed during the request. Legacy public archive posts remain, but we remove the link from them to your modern account. A non-personal account record and deletion audit timestamps remain to preserve database relationships.</p>
    <p>After confirming immediate deletion, you receive a private status receipt that remains usable after sign-out and shows when cleanup is complete. If you previously scheduled deletion under the older 30-day policy, you can sign in and cancel that request until its scheduled date. Choosing immediate deletion cannot be undone.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Queenzone is not directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect information from them.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we make material changes to this policy, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy or your data? Use the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> form, or email <a href="mailto:privacy@queenzone.org">privacy@queenzone.org</a>.</p>

  </div>
</section>
